  "outcome": "completed",
  "summary": "Design complete; product adoption unexecuted. Use the existing scoped editor for document/root callback context, retain root-relative paths and independent mounted-view constructors, flatten view composition at Plite, inherit immutable/read-only/authored policy, and reuse static readers privately in the existing cache. Admit decoration roots before caches and fast paths, propagate source definitions to automatic live owned-root mounts, and guard attribute evaluation. Widen list ordinal to existing node targets and read table path presentation through the pure grid, avoiding native indexing for known-path presentation. Keep detached conversion, annotation mapping, keyed table selection/commands and the DOM binder. Five concrete slices and final-tree type/package/browser/cost gates are recorded.",
